# Carried from the .gitignore of the repository Idiograph was split from
# (20 October 2026): the rules that reached Tools/idiograph from the root. They sit first, so the
# lines below, the app's own, still win where they say otherwise (the demo's committed recordings).
.DS_Store
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.mp4
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.pyc
~$*
.claude/
.wrangler/
# the gate's scratch folder and pytest's cache
.verify/
.pytest_cache/

.env
# the maintainer's own notes for Claude Code, beside the public CLAUDE.md (21 October 2026)
CLAUDE.local.md
__pycache__/
*.progress.json
# the Themes screen's file beside each progress file, the demo's included
*.themes.json
state.json
# Working together's keys for this computer, beside the settings when run from source (team.py)
team-device.json
agent-log.json
.agent-log.lock
# the demo's seed sidecar ships with the app, and Reset demo restores from it
!demo/pristine/Working/*.progress.json
# and so do the boards of the demo's written cases, Rowan's and Mabel's, beside them. A live
# case's own themes file stays out, as its progress file does
!demo/pristine/Working/*.themes.json
# backups an assignment or a trim on the demo writes, never part of the shipped demo
demo/*/_Archive/
# what packaging/build_mac.py and packaging/build_windows.py make: the build venv and the stage,
# then the app, the image and the installer
build/
dist/
# The demo's three recordings (recvoices, 12 November 2026), Gemini's voices joined by
# packaging/recording/voice_demo.py, the one audio committed (Adam's word, 14 October 2026) so every
# build carries it, each kept only for the transcript it was made from, with their licence and the
# tool beside them. The interviews are invented
packaging/recording/*
!packaging/recording/*-Initial-*.m4a
!packaging/recording/LICENSE-audio.md
!packaging/recording/voice_demo.py
# the GETs file at the demo's own root, and the exports the GETs screen writes there
demo/idiograph-gets.json
demo/Working/
# and the thematic analysis demo's (demos, 3 November 2026): its pristine copy's progress files ship, its live
# Themes board's file, code list, exports and backups stay out, as the IPA demo's do
!demo/ta/pristine/Working/*.progress.json
demo/ta/idiograph-gets.json
demo/ta/idiograph-codes.json
demo/ta/Working/
demo/ta/*/_Archive/
demo/ta/_Archive/
# the lock the server and the command line take around a write, in a case's Working/ and at a root
.idiograph.lock
# an agent's actions waiting for his yes at a project's root, the demo's among them, and their own lock
idiograph-holds.json
.idiograph-holds.lock
# this machine's own settings, its projects, corpus and reference paths, never shipped. A
# downloaded copy has none, and its first run writes the defaults with no project
/config.json
# and Sift's and Trace's own, run from source (20 October, the three-app split), beside it
/config.sift.json
/config.trace.json
# the record of Dangerously skip permissions beside the settings (agentlock, 2 November 2026)
/config*.skip-permissions.jsonl
/state.sift.json
/state.trace.json
# the Python environment the first run of a downloaded copy makes beside the app, and the folder it
# is set up in before it takes that name
/.venv/
/.venv-setup/
# what a build of the window (packaging/tauri) writes beside its source: cargo's target, the schemas
# and the commands' permissions tauri writes at each build, and the CLI's node_modules, none of them source
packaging/tauri/src-tauri/target/
packaging/tauri/src-tauri/gen/
packaging/tauri/src-tauri/permissions/autogenerated/
packaging/tauri/node_modules/

# the lists of real names a project replaces on import (namesrule), kept in the app folder when run from source
/names/

# the Screenshots page's clips on the website (siteclips, 12 November 2026), served by the site from its own folder
# and kept in git with it, where the launch film is copied in before each deploy
!site/holding/clips/*.mp4
